  <p>Source: each state's location list, e.g. <a href="https://www.anytimemailbox.com/l/usa/texas" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Texas</a>, <a href="https://www.anytimemailbox.com/l/usa/florida" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Florida</a>, <a href="https://www.anytimemailbox.com/l/usa/delaware" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delaware</a>. Florida's median falls between two locations, which is why it isn't a typical price ending.</p>

  <h2>Same price, different plan: five real locations</h2>
  <p>The starting price tells you little about what's included. Here are the cheapest plans at five locations, copied from their Anytime Mailbox pages:</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Location (operator)</th><th>Cheapest plan</th><th>Mail included</th><th>Open &amp; scan</th><th>Forwarding</th><th>Recipients</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Arlington, VA (TKO Suites)</td><td>Bronze $4.99/mo or $56.99/yr</td><td>15/mo</td><td>$1.00 per page</td><td>"No handling fees"</td><td>1 <Src href={S.atmArlington} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Austin, TX, 9th St (Virtual Mail Hub)</td><td>"Just an Address" $7.99/mo or $79.90/yr</td><td>None: $1.44 per incoming item</td><td>$0.18 each</td><td>$5.00 each</td><td>1 <Src href={S.atmAustin} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Omaha, NE (Advance Tax Solutions)</td><td>Bronze $9.99/mo or $109.99/yr</td><td>30/mo</td><td>$0.50 per page</td><td>$5.00 per shipping bundle</td><td>1 <Src href={S.atmOmaha} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Washington, DC, H St NE (Gold Spot Pack and Ship)</td><td>Bronze $9.99/mo or $109.99/yr</td><td>30/mo</td><td>$0.50 per page</td><td>$3.00 each</td><td>1 <Src href={S.atmDc} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Astoria, NY (Astorias Hub)</td><td>Bronze $9.99/mo or $109.99/yr</td><td>15/mo</td><td>10 pages/mo included</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>5 <Src href={S.atmAstoria} /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>What stands out:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The $4.99 plan has the priciest scans.</strong> Opening one 3-page letter at Arlington costs $3.00. That's more than half the monthly fee <Src href={S.atmArlington} />.</li>
    <li><strong>"Just an Address" charges for every piece of mail.</strong> At Austin 9th St, 10 letters a month adds $14.40 to the $7.99 fee, for a total of $22.39. The $12.99 "Address Pro" plan at the same location includes 60 items and 60 scans <Src href={S.atmAustin} />.</li>
    <li><strong>Plan names aren't standard.</strong> "Bronze" means 15 items in Arlington and Astoria, but 30 in Omaha and DC <Src href={S.atmArlington} /> <Src href={S.atmOmaha} />.</li>
    <li><strong>Yearly billing doesn't always save the same amount.</strong> Omaha's $109.99 a year compares with $119.88 for 12 monthly payments. Arlington's $56.99 compares with $59.88 <Src href={S.atmOmaha} /> <Src href={S.atmArlington} />.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The yearly-only locations</h2>
  <p>Six U.S. locations show only a yearly price, so their "starting from" number looks very high next to monthly prices. Examples are Brooklyn (495 Henry St) and Beverly Hills (Santa Monica Blvd), both at $399.99, and Overland Park, KS at $319.99. At 495 Henry St, the single plan is "Gold" at $399.99 a year. It includes 240 items a month, $0.25 per scanned page, $2.00 per forward and 5 recipients <Src href={S.atmBrooklyn} />. That's about $33 a month, not $400.</p>

  <h2>Fees that aren't on the location card</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Form 1583 notarization.</strong> Anytime Mailbox uses an online notary partner "for a nominal fee," or you can see your operator in person <Src href={S.atm1583} />. We couldn't find a published amount <Unverified note="notary fee not published" />.</li>
    <li><strong>Overage, storage, shredding and check deposit</strong> are set per plan by the operator and shown under "Full Details" before sign-up <Src href={S.atm} />. They aren't on a central price list <Unverified note="varies by location" />.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to pick an Anytime Mailbox location without overpaying</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Estimate your mail: items a month, and how many you'll want opened.</li>
    <li>Compare the full plan at two or three nearby locations, not the "starting from" price.</li>
    <li>Multiply the per-page or per-item scan fee by your usual openings. That's where cheap plans get expensive.</li>
    <li>Check whether you need more than one recipient name, since many Bronze plans include just one <Src href={S.atmDc} />.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Comparing with iPostal1, which publishes one price list for all locations? See <a href="/ipostal1-vs-anytime-mailbox/">iPostal1 vs Anytime Mailbox</a> and <a href="/ipostal1-pricing/">iPostal1 pricing explained</a>.</p>

